# Packages the lite profile leaves out of Omarchy's default set
# (book/specs/0005-memory-budget.md). The image builder skips them; on a
# machine that has them, `omarchy-lite enable --remove-packages` removes them.

# Nautilus, its extensions and previewer. It brings GTK 4, libadwaita and the
# localsearch indexer, whose XDG autostart crawls $HOME at every login.
# PCManFM (add.packages) is the file manager instead.
nautilus
nautilus-python
sushi

# Chinese, Japanese and Korean input methods. fcitx5 itself stays, for
# Omarchy's compose sequences; `omarchy setup input <method>` installs any of
# these on demand, as it does today.
fcitx5-chewing
fcitx5-chinese-addons
fcitx5-hangul
fcitx5-mozc
fcitx5-table-extra

# The resident automounter. PCManFM mounts removable media through gvfs and
# udisks when it is asked to.
udiskie
